{
  "id": "ionic_compounds_in_water___solubility_guidelines",
  "title": "Ionic Compounds in Water - Solubility Guidelines",
  "description": "Guidelines for predicting whether ionic compounds are soluble in water at room temperature. Provides solubility rules for common ions and compounds.",
  "type": "chart",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Solubility Guidelines\n\n## Usually Soluble Compounds\n- **Acetates**: Generally soluble except AgCH₃COO (moderately soluble)\n- **Ammonium salts**: NH₄⁺ compounds are soluble\n- **Chlorates & Perchlorates**: ClO₃⁻ and ClO₄⁻ compounds are soluble\n- **Group 1 Cations**: Na⁺, K⁺, Rb⁺, Cs⁺ salts are soluble\n- **Halides**: \n  - Cl⁻, Br⁻, I⁻ are generally soluble\n  - Exceptions: AgX, Hg₂X₂, PbX₂ are insoluble\n  - F⁻: MgF₂, CaF₂, SrF₂, BaF₂, PbF₂ are insoluble\n- **Nitrates & Nitrites**: NO₃⁻ and NO₂⁻ compounds are soluble\n- **Sulfates**: SO₄²⁻ compounds usually soluble\n  - Exceptions: BaSO₄, PbSO₄, HgSO₄ (insoluble)\n  - Moderately soluble: CaSO₄, SrSO₄, Ag₂SO₄\n\n## Usually Insoluble Compounds\n- **Carbonates (CO₃²⁻)**: Generally insoluble\n  - Exceptions: (NH₄)₂CO₃, Na₂CO₃, K₂CO₃\n- **Hydroxides (OH⁻)**: Generally insoluble\n  - Soluble: LiOH, NaOH, KOH, Ba(OH)₂\n  - Moderately soluble: Ca(OH)₂, Sr(OH)₂\n- **Phosphates (PO₄³⁻)**: Generally insoluble\n  - Soluble: (NH₄)₃PO₄, Na₃PO₄, K₃PO₄\n- **Sulfides (S²⁻)**: Generally insoluble\n  - Soluble: (NH₄)₂S, Na₂S, K₂S, MgS, CaS"
    },
